<<55>> Give me a writing exercise for a 6th grade student learning English. It should be an exercise on writing a report.
<<55>> You are going to write a report about the destruction of the rainforests. First, research the topic and make notes on the following questions:
\begin{enumerate}
\item Where are the world's largest rainforests?
\item Why are rainforests important?
\item Why are the rainforests being destroyed?
\item Who is responsible for the destruction?
\item How can the destruction be stopped?
\end{enumerate}
Now, write your report in your exercise book. Include the answers to the above questions and your own opinions on the destruction of the rainforests. Use some of the persuasive devices you have learned about. Try to persuade people to help stop the destruction of the rainforests.\\
Write your report.\\
When you have finished, check your work for spelling, punctuation and grammar.\\
Now, swap your report with a friend and answer the following questions about their report.
\begin{enumerate}
\item What are the writer's opinions on the destruction of the rainforests?
\item Do you think the writer has made some good points?
\item Which words and phrases show the writer's opinions?
\end{enumerate}
<<56>> Give me a writing exercise for a 2nd grade student learning English. It should be an exercise on possessive nouns.
