\item the dreams belonging to the boys \_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_
\item the eyes belonging to the fox \_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_
\item the tree belonging to the boys \_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_
\end{enumerate}
<<57>> Give me a combination of a probability exercise and a short answer exercise for a 3rd grade student learning mathematics. It should be an exercise involving explanation.
<<57>> Explain why a spinner with 3 equal sections is a fair way to choose between three options.

