<<61>> Give me a grammar exercise for a student learning Spanish. It should be an exercise on changing affirmative to negative sentences. It should be a with Answer.
<<61>> Change these affirmative sentences into negative ones.  
\begin{enumerate}
    \item Yo amo el chocolate. (I love chocolate.)
    \item Él ha jugado bien. (He played well.)
    \item Ella ha lavado los platos. (She washed the dishes.)
    \item Yo he terminado mi trabajo. (I finished my work.)
    \item Tú has ido a París. (You went to Paris.)
\end{enumerate}

\subsection*{Answers}
\begin{enumerate}
\item Yo no amo el chocolate.
\item Él no ha jugado bien.
\item Ella no ha lavado los platos.
\item Yo no he terminado mi trabajo.
\item Tú no has ido a París.
\end{enumerate}
<<62>> Give me a grammar exercise for a 2nd grade student learning English. It should be an exercise on conjunctions.
<<62>> Underline the conjunction in each sentence.
\begin{enumerate}
\item The rain poured down but the boys played on.
\item The boys played cricket because it was a sunny day.
\item The boys went home when the rain started.
\end{enumerate}
<<63>> Give me a grammar exercise for a student learning Dutch. It should be an exercise on modifying sentences.
<<63>> Change the following sentences so that they are no longer true for you. Use the following expressions:
\begin{enumerate}
\item Ik woon in Nederland. (I live in the Netherlands.)
\item Ik spreek Engels en Frans. (I speak English and French.)
\item Ik drink graag melk. (I like to drink milk.)
\item Ik draag graag een spijkerbroek. (I like to wear jeans.)
\item Ik ga graag naar de film. (I like going to the cinema.)
\end{enumerate}
<<64>> Give me a fill in the blank exercise for a student learning French. It should be an exercise on articles. It should be a with Answer.
<<64>> Compléter avec l'article partitif approprié.
\begin{enumerate}
    \item \_\_\_\_\_\_ (pain) est frais ce matin.
    \item Je prends \_\_\_\_\_\_ (tarte) à la fraise.
    \item Je mets \_\_\_\_\_\_ (poivre) et \_\_\_\_\_\_ (sel) dans mon soufflé.
    \item \_\_\_\_\_\_ (chocolat) est mauvais pour la santé.
    \item \_\_\_\_\_\_ (fromage) est délicieux avec \_\_\_\_\_\_ (raisin) et \_\_\_\_\_\_ (noix).
    \item Je prends \_\_\_\_\_\_ (thé) au citron.
    \item \_\_\_\_\_\_ (pâtes) au pesto sont délicieuses.
    \item Je mange \_\_\_\_\_\_ (fruits) le matin.
    \item \_\_\_\_\_\_ (huile) d'olive est très bonne.
    \item Je prends \_\_\_\_\_\_ (sauce) piquante avec mes frites.
\end{enumerate}

\subsection*{Answers}
\begin{enumerate}
\item Du
\item de la
\item du,\_\_\_\_\_\_ de
\item Le
\item du
\item du
\item des
\item des
\item de l'
\item de la
\end{enumerate}
<<65>> Give me a fill in the blanks exercise for a student learning French. It should be an exercise on adverbs. It should be a with Answer.
<<65>> Compléter avec un adverbe en utilisant l'inversion si nécessaire.
\begin{enumerate}
    \item Nous (dîner)          à dix-huit heures.
    \item Ils (rendre visite)          à leurs cousins ce week-end.
    \item Elle (pouvoir)          aller à la plage cet après-midi.
    \item Nous (devoir)          finir les devoirs avant la fin de la journée.
    \item Ils (vouloir)          s'installer en province.
    \item Tu (vouloir)          partir tôt?
    \item Il (vouloir)          inviter ses collègues de travail.
    \item Nous (vouloir)          vous parler de nos projets.
    \item Ils (vouloir)          passer leurs vacances à la campagne.
    \item Il (vouloir)          vendre sa maison.
\end{enumerate}

\subsection*{Answers}
\begin{enumerate}
\item dînons
\item rendent visite
\item pourra
\item devons
\item veulent
\item veux
\item veut
\item voulons
\item veulent
\item veut
\end{enumerate}
<<66>> Give me a fill in the blank exercise for a 4th grade student learning English. It should be an exercise on rhyming words.
<<66>> Fill in the blanks with rhyming words:
\begin{enumerate}
\item I like to eat \_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_.
\item The \_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_ is very cold.
\item I enjoy playing with my \_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_.
\item My room is a bit of a \_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_.
\end{enumerate}
<<67>> Give me a writing exercise for a 2nd grade student learning English. It should be an exercise about anatomy. It should be an exercise on sentence writing.
<<67>> Write a sentence about a body part. For example, "My arm hurts." Use these body parts in your sentences: head, eye, ear, nose, mouth, hand, finger, leg, foot, toe, knee, elbow, hip, shoulder, stomach, back, neck.\\

Write a sentence about a body part.\\
