<<68>> Give me a combination of an arithmetic exercise and a fill in the blank exercise for a 3rd grade student learning mathematics. It should be an exercise on measurement conversion. It should have multiple steps.
<<68>> Write in metres and centimetres.

\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item 2 m 50 cm
\item 3 m 15 cm
\item 4 m 75 cm
\item 1 m 80 cm
\item 3 m 60 cm
\item 2 m 25 cm
\end{enumerate}
<<69>> Give me a writing exercise for a student learning Dutch. It should have a subsection for answers. It should be an exercise involving an example. It should be an exercise on time.
<<69>> Say it's half past five.\\
Say it's a quarter to six.\\
Say it's a quarter past six.\\
Say it's midnight.\\
Say it's 1:45.\\

For example:\\
Hij komt om half zes.\\

\subsection*{Answers}
\begin{enumerate}
\item Het is half zes.
\item Het is kwart voor zes.
\item Het is kwart over zes.
\item Het is middernacht.
\item Het is kwart voor twee.
\end{enumerate}
