<<234>> Give me a short answer exercise for a 4th grade student learning science. It should be an exercise on sound.
<<234>> Describe the sound that you hear when you are near a busy road. Write down what the sound is like. For example, is it loud or quiet? Is it a high or low pitch? Is it a continuous sound or does it stop and start? Try to think of words to describe the sound. You could use words like: rumble, screech, hiss, whoosh, vroom, roar, crash, bang. Now, try to think of words to describe the sounds you hear in a busy street or near a railway line. Remember to think about how loud or quiet the sounds are, the pitch of the sounds and whether the sounds are continuous or do they stop and start. Write down the words you choose to describe these sounds. Finally, compare the sounds from the road, the busy street and the railway line. How are they similar? How are they different? Write down your ideas. Use your words to describe the sounds you have heard. Try to explain why you think the sounds are similar or different. Share your ideas with the class. Discuss the ideas that other learners have had. Explain which ideas you agree with and why. Explain which ideas you disagree with and why. Write down your final ideas about sound. Try to explain what sound is. Try to explain what pitch and volume are. Try to explain how sound travels from its source to your ears. Try to explain why the sound is sometimes loud and sometimes quiet. Try to explain why the pitch of a sound is sometimes high and sometimes low. Try to explain how we use our ears to help us to cross the road safely. Try to explain how the sense of touch helps us to cross the road safely. Try to explain how the sense of sight helps us to cross the road safely. Share your ideas with the class. Discuss the ideas that other learners have had. Explain which ideas you agree with and why. Explain which ideas you disagree with and why. Write down your final ideas about how we use our senses to help us to cross the road safely. Try to explain how the sense of smell helps us to cross the road safely. Try to explain how the sense of taste helps us to cross the road safely. Share your ideas with the class. Discuss the ideas that other learners have had. Explain which ideas you agree with and why. Explain which ideas you disagree with and why. Write down your final ideas about how we use our senses to help us to cross the road safely. Now, think about all the different sounds you have heard today. Try to explain why some sounds are loud and others are quiet. Try to explain why some sounds are high and others are low. Try to explain how the sounds travelled from their sources to your ears. Share your ideas with the class. Discuss the ideas that other learners have had. Explain which ideas you agree with and why. Explain which ideas you disagree with and why. Write down your final ideas about sound. Try to explain what sound is. Try to explain what pitch and volume are. Try to explain how sound travels from its source to our ears. Try to explain why the sound is sometimes loud and sometimes quiet. Try to explain why the pitch of a sound is sometimes high and sometimes low. Try to explain how we use our ears to help us to cross the road safely. Try to explain how the sense of touch helps us to cross the road safely. Try to explain how the sense of sight helps us to cross the road safely. Share your ideas with the class. Discuss the ideas that other learners have had. Explain which ideas you agree with and why. Explain which ideas you disagree with and why. Write down your final ideas about how we use our senses to help us to cross the road safely. Try to explain how the sense of smell helps us to cross the road safely. Try to explain how the sense of taste helps us to cross the road safely. Share your ideas with the class. Discuss the ideas that other learners have had. Explain which ideas you agree with and why. Explain which ideas you disagree with and why. Write down your final ideas about how we use our senses to help us to cross the road safely. Now, think about all the different sounds you