<<356>> Give me a programming exercise for a 3rd grade student learning computer science. It should have multiple steps.
<<356>> \begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item Make a program that asks your name, then says your name. 
\item Change the program so it asks your name, then says "Hello" and your name.
\end{enumerate} 
Save the file. Run the program to make sure it works. Give the file to your teacher.  

\paragraph{Bonus Question}
Change the program so it asks your name, then says "Hello" and your name, and then asks your age, and finally says "You are" and your age.  

\paragraph{Think With Me}
How could you make a program that asks your name and age and then says "Hello" and your name and "You are" and your age? Think about how you would structure the program to make it clear and easy to follow. What steps would you take to ensure that the program works as intended? Describe your thought process and how you would approach this task.  

\paragraph{Bonus Challenge}
Create a program that asks for your name and age, then says "Hello" and your name, and "You are" and your age. Save the file. Run the program to make sure it works. Give the file to your teacher. Think about how you can make the program more interesting or interactive. What additional features could you add to make it more engaging? Describe your ideas for enhancing the program.  

\paragraph{Think With Me}
Consider a program that asks for your name and age, then says "Hello" and your name, and "You are" and your age. How would you structure this program to make it clear and easy to follow? What steps would you take to ensure that the program works as intended? Describe your thought process and how you would approach this task.  

