<<537>> Give me a multiple choice exercise for a 5th grade student learning history.
<<537>> The name given to the period of time when people stopped using iron is:  
\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item the Iron Age  
\item the Bronze Age  
\item the Stone Age  
\end{enumerate}
<<538>> Give me a multiple choice exercise for a 6th grade student learning history.
<<538>> A popular game played in Tudor times was:  
\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item football  
\item tennis  
\item bowls  
\end{enumerate}  

The correct answer is:  
\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{a}  
\end{itemize}  
The other options are incorrect because:  
\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{b} Tennis was a popular sport played by the wealthy, but it was not as widely played as football.  
\item \textbf{c} Bowls was a popular game played by the upper classes, but it was not as popular as football among the general population.  
\end{itemize}  

Football was a popular game played by the common people in Tudor times, often with violent and chaotic matches. The other options, while popular among certain groups, do not accurately represent the most widely played game of the time.
