<<578>> Give me a combination of a group activity, an investigation, and a discussion exercise for a 6th grade student learning science. It should have a subsection for materials. It should be an exercise on habitats.
<<578>> \begin{enumerate}
\item Discuss with your group which habitat you will investigate.
\item Write down your predictions of what you will observe.
\item Share your predictions with the class.
\item Decide what equipment you will need and collect it.
\item Plan how you will investigate your chosen habitat.
\item Plan how you will record what you observe.
\item Show your plan and predictions to your teacher.
\item Investigate the habitat and record your observations.
\item Compare what you observed with your predictions.
\item Discuss the results with your group and try to explain what you observed.
\item Share your results, conclusions, and explanations with the class.
\end{enumerate}

\subsection*{Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item Various equipment for observing habitats (e.g., nets, jars, magnifying glasses)
\end{itemize}
