<<582>> Give me a combination of a fill in the blanks and a grammar exercise for a student learning Spanish. It should have a subsection for answers. It should be an exercise on verb forms.
<<582>> Complete the sentences below with the correct form of the verb in brackets.
\begin{enumerate}
    \item Yo \_\_ \_\_ (ir) al hospital. (I'm going to the hospital.)
    \item Nosotros \_\_ \_\_ (comer) en el restaurante. (We are eating in the restaurant.)
    \item Ella \_\_ \_\_ (bajar) por la escalera. (She's going down the stairs.)
    \item Él \_\_ \_\_ (caminar) por la calle. (He's walking down the street.)
    \item Tú \_\_ \_\_ (tomar) el taxi. (You're taking the taxi.)
\end{enumerate}

\subsection*{Answers}
\begin{enumerate}
\item Voy a ir
\item Estamos comiendo
\item Está bajando
\item Está caminando
\item Estás tomando
\end{enumerate}
