<<585>> Give me a combination of a word problem and an arithmetic exercise for a 6th grade student learning mathematics. It should be an exercise involving ratios. It should be a with Answer.
<<585>> The ratio of the number of men at a party to the number of women was \( 9 : 7 \). There were 24 more men than women. How many people were at the party?

\subsection*{Answers}
There were 87 people at the party. (42 men and 45 women)
