<<600>> Give me a question answer exercise for a student learning Dutch. It should be an exercise involving an example.
<<600>> Answer the following questions in English, following the example.
\begin{enumerate}
\item Wat is de hoofdstad van Nederland? (What is the capital of the Netherlands?)
\item Wat is de hoofdstad van Belgie? (What is the capital of Belgium?)
\item Wat is de hoofdstad van Spanje? (What is the capital of Spain?)
\item Wat is de hoofdstad van Italie? (What is the capital of Italy?)
\item Wat is de hoofdstad van Griekenland? (What is the capital of Greece?)
\item Wat is de hoofdstad van Duitsland? (What is the capital of Germany?)
\item Wat is de hoofdstad van Frankrijk? (What is the capital of France?)
\item Wat is de hoofdstad van Zwitserland? (What is the capital of Switzerland?)
\item Wat is de hoofdstad van Oostenrijk? (What is the capital of Austria?)
\item Wat is de hoofdstad van Polen? (What is the capital of Poland?)
\end{enumerate}

Example: Wat is de hoofdstad van Nederland?\\
Amsterdam is de hoofdstad van Nederland.\\
What is the capital of the Netherlands?\\
Amsterdam is the capital of the Netherlands.\\

Hint: You might want to write the answers down in a notebook or create flashcards to remember them better. You might need them later.\\

Note: The names of the countries in Dutch are the same as in English, except for Italy (Italie) and Switzerland (Zwitserland). The names of the capital cities are also the same except for Germany (Duitsland) and Poland (Polen).\\

Check your answers in an atlas or on the Internet.\\

\begin{enumerate}
\item Amsterdam
\item Brussel
\item Madrid
\item Rome
\item Athene
\item Berlijn
\item Parijs
\item Bern
\item Wenen
\item Warschau
\end{enumerate}
