<<687>> Give me a combination of a research exercise and a short answer exercise for a 3rd grade student learning geography.
<<687>> Use an atlas and reference books or the Internet to find out what the main industries are in Switzerland and Austria. What are the main exports of each country? What are the countries' main imports? Where do they come from? What are the main means of transport used to bring the imports into the countries? What are the main means of transport used to take the exports out of the countries? Are the same means of transport used for both imports and exports? If not, why not? Find out about the rivers that flow through Switzerland and Austria. Do they flow into the sea? If so, where? What are the names of the seas they flow into? What are the names of the countries these seas wash against? What are some of the main uses of these rivers? Find out about some of the main lakes in Switzerland and Austria. Where do the rivers that flow out of these lakes go? What are the names of the countries they flow through? What are some of the main uses of these rivers and lakes? Find out about the mountains in Switzerland and Austria. What are the names of the highest mountains in each country? Where are they? How high are they? What are the names of the mountain ranges they belong to? Find out about some of the countries that border Switzerland and Austria. What are the names of the countries that lie to the north, south, east and west of these two countries? What are some of the main towns and cities in these countries? What are the countries' main industries? What are the countries' main exports? Where do the exports go? What are the countries' main imports? Where do they come from? What are the main means of transport used to bring the imports into the countries? What are the main means of transport used to take the exports out of the countries? Are the same means of transport used for both imports and exports? If not, why not? Find out about the main rivers that flow through these countries. Do they flow into the sea? If so, where? What are the names of the seas they flow into? What are the names of the countries these seas wash against? What are some of the main uses of these rivers? Find out about some of the main lakes in these countries. Where do the rivers that flow out of these lakes go? What are the names of the countries they flow through? What are some of the main uses of these rivers and lakes? Find out about the main mountain ranges in these countries. What are the names of the highest mountains in each range? Where are they? How high are they? Find out about some of the main towns and cities in these countries. What are the main industries in each town and city? What are the towns' and cities' main exports? Where do they go? What are the towns' and cities' main imports? Where do they come from? What are the main means of transport used to bring the imports into the towns and cities? What are the main means of transport used to take the exports out of the towns and cities? Are the same means of transport used for both imports and exports? If not, why not? Find out about the main rivers that flow through these towns and cities. Do they flow into the sea? If so, where? What are the names of the seas they flow into? What are the names of the countries these seas wash against? What are some of the main uses of these rivers? Find out about some of the main lakes in these countries. Where do the rivers that flow out of these lakes go? What are the names of the countries they flow through? What are some of the main uses of these rivers and lakes? Find out about the main mountain ranges in these countries. What are the names of the highest mountains in each range? Where are they? How high are they? Find out about the climate and weather in Switzerland and Austria. What are the names of the large-scale maps of these countries? What are the names of the large-scale maps of the towns and cities in these countries? What is Ordnance Survey mapping? What are the names of the large-scale maps of the towns and cities in your country? What is the difference between a compass direction and a compass bearing? How do you use a compass to find the direction in which you are travelling? How do you use a compass to find the direction in which you need to travel? What is the difference between a map and a plan? What is the difference between a chart and a diagram? What is the difference between a globe and a model? What is the difference between a physical map and a relief map? What is the difference between a contour and a contour line? What is the difference between a scale drawing and a scale plan? What is the difference between an atlas and a gazetteer? What is the difference between a compass and a compass rose? What is the difference between latitude and longitude? What is the difference
<<688>> Give me a combination of a geometry exercise and a drawing exercise for a 5th grade student learning mathematics.
