An isosceles trapezium has \_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_ angles. It has two pairs of sides where one pair is \_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_ and the other pair is \_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_. The diagonals are \_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_ and the line of symmetry is \_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_.
<<689>> Give me a combination of a data collection exercise and a research exercise for a 3rd grade student learning geography.
<<689>> Carry out a survey of the weather where you live. Write down the weather every day for a week. Use symbols to show what the weather is like. Find out about the weather in other parts of the world. Use reference books or the Internet to help you. Display your results. Write a sentence or two about each place. Which place has the worst weather? Which has the best? Why? Would you like to live there? Why? Why not? Would you like to visit there? Why? Why not? What would you do there? How would you get there? How long would it take? How much would it cost? How would you send postcards to your friends and family? What would you say in your postcards? How would you take photographs? What would you take photographs of? How would you send your photographs to your friends and family? What would you buy as souvenirs? What would you give as presents when you got back home? What would you say when you got back home? What would you do when you got back home? How would you change what you do when you got back home? Why? Why not? What would you do with the photographs you took? Why? Why not? What would you do with the postcards you received? Why? Why not? What would you do with the things you bought as souvenirs? Why? Why not? What would you do with the presents you were given? Why? Why not? What would you do with the things you brought back as presents? Why? Why not? What would you do with the things you wrote, drew or painted while you were away? Why? Why not? What would you do with the stamps you collected from the places you visited? Why? Why not? What would you do with the tickets you used to get to the places you visited? Why? Why not? What would you do with the money you earned while you were away? Why? Why not? What would you do with the things you bought while you were away? Why? Why not? What would you do with the postcards you sent? Why? Why not? What would you do with the photographs you took? Why? Why not? What would you do with the reference books and the Internet pages you used to help you? Why? Why not? What would you do with the maps you used to help you? Why? Why not? What would you do with the letters you wrote while you were away? Why? Why not? What would you do with the things you brought back to show your friends and family? Why? Why not? What would you do with the things you learned while you were away? Why? Why not? What would you do with the things you saw while you were away? Why? Why not? What would you do with the things you heard while you were away? Why? Why not? What would you do with the things you smelled while you were away? Why? Why not? What would you do with the things you tasted while you were away? Why? Why not? What would you do with the things you felt while you were away? Why? Why not? What would you do with the things you said while you were away? Why? Why not? What would you do with the things you did while you were away? Why? Why not? What would you do with the things you planned while you were away? Why? Why not? What would you do with the things you hoped while you were away? Why? Why not? What would you do with the things you wished while you were away? Why? Why not? What would you do with the things you liked while you were away? Why? Why not? What would you do with the things you disliked while you were away? Why? Why not? What would you do with the things you enjoyed while you were away? Why? Why not? What would you do with the things you did not enjoy while you were away? Why? Why not? What would you do with the things you were good at while you were away? Why? Why not? What would you do with the things you were not good at while you were away? Why? Why not? What would you do with the things you learned to do while you were away? Why? Why not? What would you do with the things you did not learn to do while you were away? Why? Why not? What would you do with the things you practiced while you were away? Why? Why not? What would you do with the things you did not practice while you were away? Why? Why not? What would you do with the things you played while you were away? Why? Why not? What would you do with the things you worked while you were away? Why? Why not? What would you do with the things you rested while you were away?
