<<724>> Give me a combination of a research exercise, a mapping exercise, and an activity for a 5th grade student learning geography. It should have a subsection for materials.
<<724>> Use an atlas or the Internet to find where the world's largest cities are. Mark them on an outline map of the world.  

\subsection*{Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item An atlas or access to the Internet
\item An outline map of the world
\end{itemize}  
Now answer these questions about the cities you have found:  
\begin{enumerate}
\item Which are the ten largest cities in the world?  
\item Where are they?  
\item Are they all on the coast or are some inland?  
\item How many people live in each of these cities?  
\item How many of these cities are in Asia?  
\end{enumerate}  

\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item What are the names of the largest cities in Asia?  
\item Where are they?  
\item How many people live in each of these cities?  
\end{enumerate}  

\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item What are the names of the largest cities in North America?  
\item Where are they?  
\item How many people live in each of these cities?  
\end{enumerate}  

\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item What are the names of the largest cities in South America?  
\item Where are they?  
\item How many people live in each of these cities?  
\end{enumerate}  

\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item What are the names of the largest cities in Europe?  
\item Where are they?  
\item How many people live in each of these cities?  
\end{enumerate}  

\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item What are the names of the largest cities in Africa?  
\item Where are they?  
\item How many people live in each of these cities?  
\end{enumerate}  

\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item What are the names of the largest cities in Australia and Oceania?  
\item Where are they?  
\item How many people live in each of these cities?  
\end{enumerate}  

\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item What are the names of the largest cities in the Middle East?  
\item Where are they?  
\item How many people live in each of these cities?  
\end{enumerate}  

\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item What are the names of the largest cities in Russia and the countries of the former Soviet Union?  
\item Where are they?  
\item How many people live in each of these cities?  
\end{enumerate}  

Now use the information you have collected to write a short report about the world's largest cities. Include in your report the answers to the questions above. You should also say what you think makes these cities so large. Is it because they are important ports, the countries' capital cities, or because they are in a good position for trade? Say what you think the problems are in these cities and how the cities could be improved. You could include some ideas for new towns or cities.  

\subsection*{Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item Paper and writing tools (pens, pencils, etc.)
\end{itemize}  



\begin{enumerate}
\item \textbf{What is a large city?}  
\item \textbf{How are large cities formed?}  
\item \textbf{Why are large cities built where they are?}  
\item \textbf{What problems do large cities have?}  
\item \textbf{How can large cities be improved?}  
\end{enumerate}  

\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item How are new towns created?  
\item Where are they built?  
\item What are they like?  
\item What are the benefits of new towns?  
\end{enumerate}  

\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item How can slums be improved?  
\item What is being done to improve slums in some large cities?  
\end{enumerate}  

\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item What is a megacity?  
\item Where are the world's megacities?  
\item What problems do megacities have?  
\item How can megacities be improved?  
\end{enumerate}  

\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item What is urbanisation?  
\item Why do people move from the country to towns and cities?  
\item What are the problems of urbanisation?  
\end{enumerate}  

\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item What is suburbanisation
