<<741>> Give me a combination of a word problem and an arithmetic exercise for a 3rd grade student learning mathematics. It should be an exercise involving ratios.
<<741>> The ratio of the amount of coffee to the amount of milk in a coffee drink is \( 1 : 3 \). If I use 30 ml of milk, how much coffee should I add? How much coffee drink will I have in total? Show your method: \_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_.

\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item How much coffee should be added?
\item What is the total amount of coffee drink?
\end{enumerate}
<<742>> Give me a combination of an arithmetic exercise and a word problem for a 3rd grade student learning mathematics. It should be an exercise involving weight calculation. It should have multiple steps.
