<<749>> Give me a combination of an arithmetic exercise and a fill in the blank exercise for a 3rd grade student learning mathematics. It should be an exercise on comparing fractions. It should have multiple steps.
<<749>> Compare the following fractions by writing \( < \) or \( > \) in the blank space.

\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item \( \frac{1}{2} \) \_\_ \( \frac{1}{3} \)
\item \( \frac{3}{4} \) \_\_ \( \frac{2}{3} \)
\item \( \frac{2}{5} \) \_\_ \( \frac{3}{10} \)
\item \( \frac{4}{7} \) \_\_ \( \frac{1}{2} \)
\item \( \frac{5}{12} \) \_\_ \( \frac{1}{3} \)
\item \( \frac{7}{8} \) \_\_ \( \frac{2}{3} \)
