<<851>> Give me a combination of a drawing exercise and an activity for a 1st grade student learning computer science.
<<851>> Draw a picture of a robot. What features would you give your robot? Describe your robot in detail. What would you name it? What colors would it have? What shape would it be? Would it have any special abilities or tools? Think about what your robot could do. What would it be used for? Describe the tasks it would perform. How would it move? Would it have legs, wheels, or something else? Think about how your robot would sense the world. Would it have eyes, ears, or a nose? How would it communicate with people? Would it talk or use another method? Draw your robot and label its parts. Describe the features and abilities you designed for your robot. Think about how you would teach your robot to perform tasks. Would you use rewards or another method? Describe how you would teach your robot. Consider the responsibilities that come with creating a robot. What kind of robot would you not want to exist? Why? What kind of robot would you want to exist? Why? Describe the robot you would want or not want to exist and explain your reasons. Reflect on what you learned about robots. What did you find interesting or surprising? Describe your thoughts and feelings about robots. Think about how robots could be used in your community. Describe how robots could help people in your area. Imagine you are an engineer designing a robot for your community. What kind of robot would you create? Describe the robot you would design and its features. Think about how you would test your robot to ensure it works properly. Describe the process you would use to test your robot. Reflect on what you learned about creating and testing robots. What did you find interesting or surprising? Describe your thoughts and feelings about designing and testing robots. Consider the benefits and drawbacks of using robots in your community. Describe the advantages and disadvantages you think robots would have. Think about how you would explain the benefits of robots to someone who is unsure about them. Describ